comments.body:
@tghosth this is not a session management issue. I would think that https://github.com/OWASP/ASVS/blob/master/4.0/en/0x11-V2-Authentication.md would have a mention, but I cannot find one.

A well known security vendor had this issue last year in which they were not properly checking against ALL data a user was asserting during authentication. They were only doing partial checking.

If the assertion contained username, password, and token, the security vendor was only checking on username and password. It's one of these simple overlooked issues like "is it plugged in".
